        "### 7. Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "-   **Final Outcome**: The project successfully develops a Logistic Regression model capable of predicting child survival risk based on maternal and household factors. It integrates this model into an interactive system that provides both rule-based and LLM-powered health recommendations.\n",
        "\n",
        "-   **Objective Achieved**: The primary objective of predicting child survival and offering personalized advice has been largely achieved. The model demonstrates high overall accuracy, though there's room for improvement in identifying the minority 'at-risk' class.\n",
        "\n",
        "-   **Limitations**:\n",
        "    -   **Class Imbalance**: The dataset's severe class imbalance makes it challenging for the model to achieve very high recall for the 'at-risk' class without potentially sacrificing precision for the 'healthy' class.\n",
        "    -   **Model Complexity**: Logistic Regression is a linear model; more complex non-linear relationships might not be fully captured. More advanced models (e.g., gradient boosting, neural networks) could potentially improve performance.\n",
        "    -   **LLM Dependency**: The advanced AI recommendations depend on the availability and configuration of the Google Gemini API key. Without it, only rule-based recommendations are provided.\n",
        "    -   **Feature Interpretability vs. Causation**: While feature importance shows correlation, it does not imply direct causation. Recommendations should be interpreted as general health advice based on statistical patterns.\n",
        "    -   **Generalizability**: The model is trained on NFHS-5 data from India. Its performance and recommendations might not directly generalize to other populations or regions without re-training and validation."
      ]
